o retry, and if retrying, produce the next attempt number and a memory append with the reflection from the last failed attempt. If success or max reached, finalize with null memory.\n\nFrom typical agent frameworks, after each failure, the agent records a reflection and then retries. When success, it stops. When max attempts exhausted, it stops without further reflection? Or maybe it reflects anyway? The schema allows null, so we can set null for stop cases.\n\nNow about next_attempt: If we decide to continue, we need to provide an integer. The integer could be the number of attempts so far? Or the next attempt index? In many iterative algorithms, the attempt count increments. In the fixtures, attempts array length indicates number of attempts. For case 001, attempts length=3, so next_attempt should be 4 (the fourth attempt). For case 000, attempts length=1, but success, so we don't need a next attempt, maybe 0. For case 002, length=4, max=4, stop, so 0 or maybe 4? But next_attempt is required integer, must be something.\n\nWe need to see if there's any pattern from the case IDs or nonce? Probably not.\n\nAnother angle: The task name \"RF-02\" might correspond to \"Reflection Feedback\" version 2. Possibly the logic is: if the last attempt succeeded, decision=\"finalize\", memory_append=null, next_attempt=attempts_count (maybe to indicate no more). If last attempt failed and attempts_count < max_attempts, decision=\"continue\", memory_append = {reflection: last_reflection, signature: last_failure_signature}, next_attempt = attempts_count + 1. If last attempt failed and attempts_count >= max_attempts, decision=\"stop\", memory_append=null, next_attempt=attempts_count (or 0). But we need to be consistent with the requirement \"Do not expect case_id, seed, or any outer fixture-row keys; use only fields present in the payload object.\" So we only have payload fields.\n\nThus the implementation: read attempts list, max_attempts. Determine last attempt. If any attempt has